  "question": {
    "text": "If the number of seven-digit numbers, such that the sum of their digits is even, is $m \\cdot n \\cdot 10^{\\mathrm{n}}$; $m, n \\in\\{1,2,3, \\ldots, 9\\}$, then $m+n$ is equal to _______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "14",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Total 7 digit nos. $=9000000$<br/>7 digit nos. having sum of digits<br/>Even $=4500000$<br/>$=9.5 \\cdot 10^5$<br/>$\\mathrm{m}=9, \\mathrm{n}=5$<br/>$\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{n}=14$",
    "image": null
  },
